    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-301-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "301 13  Emergency determinations—serious drugs",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-1-sec-301-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that:\n\n(a) a substance, other than a growing plant, is a controlled drug\nor a border controlled drug; or\n\n(b) a growing plant is a controlled plant or a border controlled\nplant.\n\n(2) The Minister must not make a determination under subsection (1)\nunless he or she is satisfied:\n\n(a) that there is an imminent and substantial risk that the\nsubstance or plant will be taken without appropriate medical\nsupervision; and\n\n(b) one or more of the following conditions is met:\n\n(i) taking the substance or plant may create a risk of death\nor serious harm;\n\n(ii) taking the substance or plant may have a physical or\nmental effect substantially similar to that caused by\ntaking a listed serious drug;\n\n(iii) there is limited or no known lawful use of the substance\nor plant in Australia, and the substance or plant has been\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSerious drugs  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012\nNo. 167, 2012            15\nfound by a public official in the course of the\nperformance of the official’s duties;\n\n(iv) the substance or plant may pose a substantial risk to the\nhealth or safety of the public.\n\n(3) The Minister must not make more than one determination under\nthis section in relation to a particular substance or plant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that:\n\n(a) a substance, other than a growing plant, is a controlled drug\nor a border controlled drug; or\n\n(b) a growing plant is a controlled plant or a border controlled\nplant.\n\n(2) The Minister must not make a determination under subsection (1)\nunless he or she is satisfied:\n\n(a) that there is an imminent and substantial risk that the\nsubstance or plant will be taken without appropriate medical\nsupervision; and\n\n(b) one or more of the following conditions is met:\n\n(i) taking the substance or plant may create a risk of death\nor serious harm;\n\n(ii) taking the substance or plant may have a physical or\nmental effect substantially similar to that caused by\ntaking a listed serious drug;\n\n(iii) there is limited or no known lawful use of the substance\nor plant in Australia, and the substance or plant has been\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSerious drugs  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012\nNo. 167, 2012            15\nfound by a public official in the course of the\nperformance of the official’s duties;\n\n(iv) the substance or plant may pose a substantial risk to the\nhealth or safety of the public.\n\n(3) The Minister must not make more than one determination under\nthis section in relation to a particular substance or plant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-301-19-ss-1"
