    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-301-22",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "301 16  Emergency determinations—effectiveness",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-1-sec-301-22"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under this Subdivision in relation to a substance\n(including a growing plant) or a quantity of such a substance has\neffect:\n\n(a) from the time the determination is registered (within the\nmeaning of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003); and\n\n(b) for the period of 12 months from that registration, or such\nshorter period as is specified in the determination, as\nextended (if at all) under subsection (2).\n\n(2) If exceptional circumstances prevent the listing (by regulation) of\nthe substance or quantity, to the same effect, the Minister may, by\nlegislative instrument, extend the period during which the\ndetermination is in force by a further period or periods.\n\n(3) The Minister must not extend the period under subsection (2) with\nthe effect that the determination would stay in force for longer than\n18 months after the time the determination is registered (within the\nmeaning of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003).\n\n(4) A determination made under this Subdivision has no effect to the\nextent that it is inconsistent with a regulation made for the\npurposes of Subdivision A.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A determination under this Subdivision in relation to a substance\n(including a growing plant) or a quantity of such a substance has\neffect:\n\n(a) from the time the determination is registered (within the\nmeaning of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003); and\n\n(b) for the period of 12 months from that registration, or such\nshorter period as is specified in the determination, as\nextended (if at all) under subsection (2).\n\n(2) If exceptional circumstances prevent the listing (by regulation) of\nthe substance or quantity, to the same effect, the Minister may, by\nlegislative instrument, extend the period during which the\ndetermination is in force by a further period or periods.\n\n(3) The Minister must not extend the period under subsection (2) with\nthe effect that the determination would stay in force for longer than\n18 months after the time the determination is registered (within the\nmeaning of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003).\n\n(4) A determination made under this Subdivision has no effect to the\nextent that it is inconsistent with a regulation made for the\npurposes of Subdivision A.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-301-22-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-301-22-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-301-22-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-301-22-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0a55ed5d0e34fddd2b33b500d0f3b2920c034f31479d3676d5b0018894909af4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-1-sec-301-22",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "301 16  Emergency determinations—effectiveness",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A determination under this Subdivision in relation to a substance\n(including a growing plant) or a quantity of such a substance has\neffect:\n\n(a) from the time the determination is registered (within the\nmeaning of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003); and\n\n(b) for the period of 12 months from that registration, or such\nshorter period as is specified in the determination, as\nextended (if at all) under subsection (2).\n\n(2) If exceptional circumstances prevent the listing (by regulation) of\nthe substance or quantity, to the same effect, the Minister may, by\nlegislative instrument, extend the period during which the\ndetermination is in force by a further period or periods.\n\n(3) The Minister must not extend the period under subsection (2) with\nthe effect that the determination would stay in force for longer than\n18 months after the time the determination is registered (within the\nmeaning of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003).\n\n(4) A determination made under this Subdivision has no effect to the\nextent that it is inconsistent with a regulation made for the\npurposes of Subdivision A."
    },
