        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Transitional—listing of existing serious drugs and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-1-sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "precursors by regulation\n(1)\nThis item applies in relation to a substance or plant that, immediately\nbefore the commencement of this item, was listed under Division 314 of\nthe Criminal Code as belonging to any of the following classes of\nsubstances or plants (the substance’s or plant’s Criminal Code class):\n\n(a) a controlled drug;\n\n(b) a controlled plant;\n\n(c) a controlled precursor;\n\n(d) a border controlled drug;\n\n(e) a border controlled plant;\n\n(f) a border controlled precursor.\n(2)\nSections 301.7 and 301.8 of the Criminal Code, as amended by Part 1 of\nthis Schedule, do not apply in relation to a regulation made for the\npurposes of Subdivision A of Division 301 of the Criminal Code (as so\namended) listing the substance or plant as belonging to the same\nCriminal Code class as that to which it belonged immediately before the\ncommencement of this item.\nNote 1: Sections 301.7 and 301.8 of the Criminal Code, as so amended, provide that some\nconditions must be satisfied before new regulations can be made listing a substance or\nplant as belonging to a Criminal Code class.\nNote 2: For the commencement of this item, see section 2 of this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nIdentity crime and air travel  Schedule 2\nIdentity crime  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012\nNo. 167, 2012            19",
      "skos:definition": "precursors by regulation\n(1)\nThis item applies in relation to a substance or plant that, immediately\nbefore the commencement of this item, was listed under Division 314 of\nthe Criminal Code as belonging to any of the following classes of\nsubstances or plants (the substance’s or plant’s Criminal Code class):\n\n(a) a controlled drug;\n\n(b) a controlled plant;\n\n(c) a controlled precursor;\n\n(d) a border controlled drug;\n\n(e) a border controlled plant;\n\n(f) a border controlled precursor.\n(2)\nSections 301.7 and 301.8 of the Criminal Code, as amended by Part 1 of\nthis Schedule, do not apply in relation to a regulation made for the\npurposes of Subdivision A of Division 301 of the Criminal Code (as so\namended) listing the substance or plant as belonging to the same\nCriminal Code class as that to which it belonged immediately before the\ncommencement of this item.\nNote 1: Sections 301.7 and 301.8 of the Criminal Code, as so amended, provide that some\nconditions must be satisfied before new regulations can be made listing a substance or\nplant as belonging to a Criminal Code class.\nNote 2: For the commencement of this item, see section 2 of this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nIdentity crime and air travel  Schedule 2\nIdentity crime  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012\nNo. 167, 2012            19",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-24-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b29cf55e9ed1f43cfc13de0deb3d86911283ff775a0930479e6ee1f0d45640f9",
      "skos:note": "Listing of existing serious drugs and precursors by regulation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-1-sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Transitional—listing of existing serious drugs and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "precursors by regulation\n(1)\nThis item applies in relation to a substance or plant that, immediately\nbefore the commencement of this item, was listed under Division 314 of\nthe Criminal Code as belonging to any of the following classes of\nsubstances or plants (the substance’s or plant’s Criminal Code class):\n\n(a) a controlled drug;\n\n(b) a controlled plant;\n\n(c) a controlled precursor;\n\n(d) a border controlled drug;\n\n(e) a border controlled plant;\n\n(f) a border controlled precursor.\n(2)\nSections 301.7 and 301.8 of the Criminal Code, as amended by Part 1 of\nthis Schedule, do not apply in relation to a regulation made for the\npurposes of Subdivision A of Division 301 of the Criminal Code (as so\namended) listing the substance or plant as belonging to the same\nCriminal Code class as that to which it belonged immediately before the\ncommencement of this item.\nNote 1: Sections 301.7 and 301.8 of the Criminal Code, as so amended, provide that some\nconditions must be satisfied before new regulations can be made listing a substance or\nplant as belonging to a Criminal Code class.\nNote 2: For the commencement of this item, see section 2 of this Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nIdentity crime and air travel  Schedule 2\nIdentity crime  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012\nNo. 167, 2012            19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-24-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-1-sec-24"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-370",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "370 2  Definition of foreign indictable offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-370"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "In Division 372:\nforeign indictable offence means an offence against a law of a\nforeign country or part of a foreign country that is constituted by\nconduct that, if engaged in in Australia, would constitute an\nindictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "In Division 372:\nforeign indictable offence means an offence against a law of a\nforeign country or part of a foreign country that is constituted by\nconduct that, if engaged in in Australia, would constitute an\nindictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-370-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-370-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-370-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "007c87549963654bf52ea5b5008ca54a3ad8631cf96344f09dfedc797a194127",
      "skos:note": "Defines foreign indictable offence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-370",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "370 2  Definition of foreign indictable offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "In Division 372:\nforeign indictable offence means an offence against a law of a\nforeign country or part of a foreign country that is constituted by\nconduct that, if engaged in in Australia, would constitute an\nindictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-370-norm",
