    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-370-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "370 3  Concurrent operation intended",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-370-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Part is not intended to exclude or limit the concurrent\noperation of any law of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Part is not intended to exclude\nor limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory\nthat makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Part; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the State or Territory.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does\nany one or more of the following:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Part;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nunder this Part;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This Part is not intended to exclude or limit the concurrent\noperation of any law of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Part is not intended to exclude\nor limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory\nthat makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Part; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the State or Territory.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does\nany one or more of the following:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Part;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nunder this Part;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-370-2-ss-1"
