    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372(3) 1A  Dealing in identification information that involves use of a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-372-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person obtains identification information; and\n\n(b) the first person does so using a carriage service; and\n\n(c) the first person deals in the identification information; and\n\n(d) the first person intends that any person (the user) (whether or\nnot the first person) will use the identification information to\npretend to be, or to pass the user off as, another person\n(whether living, dead, real or fictitious) for the purpose of:\n\n(i) committing an offence; or\n\n(ii) facilitating the commission of an offence; and\n\n(e) the offence referred to in paragraph (d) is:\n\n(i) an indictable offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n\n(ii) an indictable offence against a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(iii) a foreign indictable offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\nNote:\nDeal, in identification information, includes make, supply or use any\nsuch information. See section 370.1.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person obtains identification information; and\n\n(b) the first person does so using a carriage service; and\n\n(c) the first person deals in the identification information; and\n\n(d) the first person intends that any person (the user) (whether or\nnot the first person) will use the identification information to\npretend to be, or to pass the user off as, another person\n(whether living, dead, real or fictitious) for the purpose of:\n\n(i) committing an offence; or\n\n(ii) facilitating the commission of an offence; and\n\n(e) the offence referred to in paragraph (d) is:\n\n(i) an indictable offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n\n(ii) an indictable offence against a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(iii) a foreign indictable offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\nNote:\nDeal, in identification information, includes make, supply or use any\nsuch information. See section 370.1.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "49bfe98ec3a3272c930038eebf8c8ef535db2e34f026a82349f9e2be9121eb83",
      "skos:note": "Dealing in identification information using a carriage service is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-372-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372(3) 1A  Dealing in identification information that involves use of a",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the first person obtains identification information; and\n\n(b) the first person does so using a carriage service; and\n\n(c) the first person deals in the identification information; and\n\n(d) the first person intends that any person (the user) (whether or\nnot the first person) will use the identification information to\npretend to be, or to pass the user off as, another person\n(whether living, dead, real or fictitious) for the purpose of:\n\n(i) committing an offence; or\n\n(ii) facilitating the commission of an offence; and\n\n(e) the offence referred to in paragraph (d) is:\n\n(i) an indictable offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth; or\n\n(ii) an indictable offence against a law of a State or\nTerritory; or\n\n(iii) a foreign indictable offence.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\nNote:\nDeal, in identification information, includes make, supply or use any\nsuch information. See section 370.1."
    },
