    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372(5) 1A  Dealing in identification information that involves use of a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-372-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the prosecution proves beyond reasonable doubt that a person\nengaged in the conduct referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (3)(a),\nthen it is presumed, unless the person proves to the contrary, that\nthe person used a carriage service to engage in that conduct.\nNote:\nA defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection. See section 13.4.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the prosecution proves beyond reasonable doubt that a person\nengaged in the conduct referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (3)(a),\nthen it is presumed, unless the person proves to the contrary, that\nthe person used a carriage service to engage in that conduct.\nNote:\nA defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection. See section 13.4.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e5275c62044c63302087c52ed6c4686a5399001e7990ade3aa316f73db60d002",
      "skos:note": "Presumption of carriage service use in conduct involving identification information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-372-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372(5) 1A  Dealing in identification information that involves use of a",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the prosecution proves beyond reasonable doubt that a person\nengaged in the conduct referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (3)(a),\nthen it is presumed, unless the person proves to the contrary, that\nthe person used a carriage service to engage in that conduct.\nNote:\nA defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this\nsubsection. See section 13.4.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel"
    },
