    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-3ul",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3UL Definitions—Division 3B",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-3ul"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "In this Division:\nconstitutional airport means:\n\n(a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the\nCrimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or\n\n(b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory.\ngovernment photographic identity document means an identity\ndocument providing photographic identification of a person that is\nissued by:\n\n(a) the government of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory;\nor\n\n(b) the government of a foreign country or part of a foreign\ncountry.\nidentity document:\n\n(a) means a document (such as a driver’s licence, birth\ncertificate, credit card or identity card) that evidences or\nindicates, or can be used to evidence or indicate, a person’s\nidentity or any aspect of a person’s identity; but\n\n(b) does not include a document prescribed by regulation for the\npurposes of this definition.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "skos:definition": "In this Division:\nconstitutional airport means:\n\n(a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the\nCrimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or\n\n(b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory.\ngovernment photographic identity document means an identity\ndocument providing photographic identification of a person that is\nissued by:\n\n(a) the government of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory;\nor\n\n(b) the government of a foreign country or part of a foreign\ncountry.\nidentity document:\n\n(a) means a document (such as a driver’s licence, birth\ncertificate, credit card or identity card) that evidences or\nindicates, or can be used to evidence or indicate, a person’s\nidentity or any aspect of a person’s identity; but\n\n(b) does not include a document prescribed by regulation for the\npurposes of this definition.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-3ul-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-3ul-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd12dea544ad89a6994e05094facbd65b781121e499984d736cdb822f6d11283",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms for Division 3B"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-3ul",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3UL Definitions—Division 3B",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "In this Division:\nconstitutional airport means:\n\n(a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the\nCrimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or\n\n(b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory.\ngovernment photographic identity document means an identity\ndocument providing photographic identification of a person that is\nissued by:\n\n(a) the government of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory;\nor\n\n(b) the government of a foreign country or part of a foreign\ncountry.\nidentity document:\n\n(a) means a document (such as a driver’s licence, birth\ncertificate, credit card or identity card) that evidences or\nindicates, or can be used to evidence or indicate, a person’s\nidentity or any aspect of a person’s identity; but\n\n(b) does not include a document prescribed by regulation for the\npurposes of this definition.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel"
    },
