    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-3un",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3UN Identity information at airports—offences relating to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-3un"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "section 3UM\nOffence by suspect\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a constable makes a request of the person under subsection\n3UM(3); and\n\n(b) the person fails to comply with the request; and\n\n(c) the constable complies with subsection 3UM(4).\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote:\nThe following more serious offences may also apply:\n(a) giving false or misleading information (see section 137.1 of the\nCriminal Code);\n(b) producing a false or misleading document (see section 137.2 of\nthe Criminal Code);\n(c) obstructing a Commonwealth public official (see section 149.1 of\nthe Criminal Code).\n\n(2) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(a) and (c).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "skos:definition": "section 3UM\nOffence by suspect\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) a constable makes a request of the person under subsection\n3UM(3); and\n\n(b) the person fails to comply with the request; and\n\n(c) the constable complies with subsection 3UM(4).\nPenalty: 20 penalty units.\nNote:\nThe following more serious offences may also apply:\n(a) giving false or misleading information (see section 137.1 of the\nCriminal Code);\n(b) producing a false or misleading document (see section 137.2 of\nthe Criminal Code);\n(c) obstructing a Commonwealth public official (see section 149.1 of\nthe Criminal Code).\n\n(2) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(a) and (c).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 2  Identity crime and air travel",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-3un-ss-1"
