      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "Offence by constable\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection\n3UM(4); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty: 5 penalty units.\n\n(4) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\nCriminal Code Act 1995",
      "skos:definition": "Offence by constable\n\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection\n3UM(4); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the conduct breaches the requirement.\nPenalty: 5 penalty units.\n\n(4) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.\nCriminal Code Act 1995",
      "cml:hasPart": [
