      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-376-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "376 2  False identification information—at constitutional airports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-376-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the defendant) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the defendant uses information at a place; and\n\n(b) the defendant does so reckless as to whether the information\nis used to identify the defendant as a passenger on a flight;\nand\n\n(c) the information is identification information; and\n\n(d) the information is false in relation to the defendant; and\n\n(e) the place is a constitutional airport.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(e).\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\n\n(3) In this section:\nconstitutional airport means:\n\n(a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the\nCrimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or\n\n(b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person (the defendant) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the defendant uses information at a place; and\n\n(b) the defendant does so reckless as to whether the information\nis used to identify the defendant as a passenger on a flight;\nand\n\n(c) the information is identification information; and\n\n(d) the information is false in relation to the defendant; and\n\n(e) the place is a constitutional airport.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(e).\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2.\n\n(3) In this section:\nconstitutional airport means:\n\n(a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the\nCrimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or\n\n(b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory.",
