    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Amendments made by Part 2",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDivision 3B of Part IAA of the Crimes Act 1914, as inserted by Part 2\nof this Schedule, applies in relation to persons reasonably suspected of\noffences whether the offences are suspected of having been committed\nbefore, on or after the commencement of this item.\n(2)\nDivision 376 of the Criminal Code, as inserted by Part 2 of this\nSchedule, applies in relation to conduct and circumstances arising on or\nafter the commencement of this item.\nNote:\nThis item commences on the day after this Act receives the Royal Assent (see\nsection 2).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 3  Other measures",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nDivision 3B of Part IAA of the Crimes Act 1914, as inserted by Part 2\nof this Schedule, applies in relation to persons reasonably suspected of\noffences whether the offences are suspected of having been committed\nbefore, on or after the commencement of this item.\n(2)\nDivision 376 of the Criminal Code, as inserted by Part 2 of this\nSchedule, applies in relation to conduct and circumstances arising on or\nafter the commencement of this item.\nNote:\nThis item commences on the day after this Act receives the Royal Assent (see\nsection 2).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 3  Other measures",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-10-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-10-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "035de9f436c3661aa43dcf77d9fc790b28d085b82b74d02a20f3c51c9a70837f",
      "skos:note": "Division 3B of Part IAA of the Crimes Act 1914 applies to persons reasonably suspected of offences."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012#sch-2-sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 Amendments made by Part 2",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDivision 3B of Part IAA of the Crimes Act 1914, as inserted by Part 2\nof this Schedule, applies in relation to persons reasonably suspected of\noffences whether the offences are suspected of having been committed\nbefore, on or after the commencement of this item.\n(2)\nDivision 376 of the Criminal Code, as inserted by Part 2 of this\nSchedule, applies in relation to conduct and circumstances arising on or\nafter the commencement of this item.\nNote:\nThis item commences on the day after this Act receives the Royal Assent (see\nsection 2).\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167\n\nSchedule 3  Other measures"
    },
